      "writtenOn": "2026-10-07T12:22:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the check is gone. `PldmFruDecorators` creates each interface on first use, so the caller only sets the property. If creating an interface fails, the class logs it once, removes the interfaces it already created for that terminus and creates no more.\n\nIt does not report the failure to the caller, which has nothing useful to do with it; `createInventoryPath` likewise only logs a failure, and its callers do not act on it.",
      "parentUuid": "cdc30516_3a6023d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 750,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 753,
        "endChar": 21
      },
